  "reviewed_interpretation": "The single authoritative I035 execution is valid and terminal. Fresh target authority, causal target/anchor semantics, fixed horizons, mirror accounting and exact shipping mirrors all passed. The I034 response-amplitude deficit is not explained by lack of fast-update opportunity. Across fixed horizons 1/2/4/8, the median slow-update bin fraction is only about 4.7-5.6% while the median fast-update bin fraction is about 94.4-95.3%. The fast branch contributes about 99.8-99.9% of absolute tracker estimate movement, yet the median response deficit remains 4.29/5.30/5.15/2.55 dB. Slow-update exposure is descriptively negatively associated with response deficit at all fixed horizons (Spearman about -0.27 to -0.40), rather than positively associated as a simple slow-gating explanation would suggest. At h8, fast absolute contribution and total absolute update opportunity are positively associated with response deficit (about +0.43 and +0.45). These descriptive associations do not establish causality, but they reject a simple 'too many slow-update bins' explanation and provide no basis to tune alpha or the 0.35 branch threshold. The remaining mechanism question is whether all-bin noise-estimate aggregation and spectral/domain transfer dilute or misalign the speech-band tracker movement relative to post-NS local observation energy.",
